<p> The histogram illustrates the distribution of compressive strength acro=
ss the concrete dataset.</p>
<p> The majority of observations are concentrated between approximately 20 =
and 50 MPa, with the highest frequency occurring around 30=E2=80=9340 MPa.<=
/p>
<p> The distribution exhibits a slight positive (right) skew, as the tail e=
xtends towards higher compressive strength values.</p>
<p> The descriptive statistics support this observation, with a mean streng=
th of 35.82 MPa and a median of 34.45 MPa.</p>
<p> The strength values range from 2.33 MPa to 82.60 MPa, indicating consid=
erable variation across the concrete mixtures.</p>
<p> <strong>Conclusion:</strong> Concrete compressive strength is not perfe=
ctly normally distributed and exhibits a slight right-skewed distribution.<=
/p>
