oor predictive performance.</p>
<p> Linear Regression performed considerably better, achieving an MAE of 5.=
33 MPa, RMSE of 6.79 MPa and R=C2=B2 of 0.801.</p>
<p> Random Forest achieved the best performance, with an MAE of 3.49 MPa, R=
MSE of 4.55 MPa and R=C2=B2 of 0.911. This indicates that it explains appro=
ximately 91.1% of the variation in compressive strength in the test dataset=
.</p>
<p> Random Forest was therefore selected as the preferred model because it =
achieved the lowest prediction errors and highest R=C2=B2 score among the t=
hree models.</p>
