=3D"=CD=BCr"> 4. Importance of Water-to-Cement Ratio</span></div><div class=
=3D"cm-line">The water-to-cement ratio had a correlation of approximately <=
span class=3D"=CD=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</span><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a">-0.489</s=
pan><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</span> with compressive strength, i=
ndicating that higher ratios were generally associated with lower strength.=
 Its relationship was slightly stronger in absolute terms than cement alone=
 (0.488), demonstrating the importance of considering ingredient proportion=
s rather than individual quantities in isolation.</div><div class=3D"cm-lin=
e"><br></div><div class=3D"cm-line"><span class=3D"=CD=BCr =CD=BCp">###</sp=
an><span class=3D"=CD=BCr"> 5. Model Performance</span></div><div class=3D"=
