training and testing split. The mean baseline performed poorly, while Linea=
r Regression achieved an R=C2=B2 of <span class=3D"=CD=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</sp=
an><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a">0.801</span><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a =CD=BCp">**=
</span> and Random Forest achieved an R=C2=B2 of <span class=3D"=CD=BC1a =
=CD=BCp">**</span><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a">0.911</span><span class=3D"=CD=
=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</span>.</div><div class=3D"cm-line"><br></div><div class=
=3D"cm-line"> Random Forest produced the best results, with an MAE of <span=
 class=3D"=CD=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</span><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a">3.49 MPa</spa=
n><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</span> and RMSE of <span class=3D"=CD=
=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</span><span class=3D"=CD=BC1a">4.55 MPa</span><span class=
=3D"=CD=BC1a =CD=BCp">**</span>, demonstrating its ability to capture more =
complex relationships in the dataset than the linear model.</div><div class=
=3D"cm-line"><br></div><div class=3D"cm-line"><span class=3D"=CD=BCr =CD=BC=
p">###</span><span class=3D"=CD=BCr"> 6. Largest Prediction Errors</span></=
div><div class=3D"cm-line"> The model's largest errors included underpredic=
tion of some high-strength concrete samples and overprediction of some lowe=
r-strength samples. Some difficult predictions also involved early curing a=
ges. This suggests that the model is less accurate at certain extremes and =
that prediction errors are not evenly distributed across all concrete mixes=
.</div><div class=3D"cm-line"><br></div><div class=3D"cm-line"><span class=
