=BCp">###</span><span class=3D"=CD=BCr"> Overall Conclusion</span></div><di=
v class=3D"cm-line"> The findings demonstrate that concrete compressive str=
ength is influenced by multiple interacting factors, particularly cement co=
ntent, water-to-cement ratio and curing age. Random Forest provided the str=
ongest predictive performance among the models evaluated.</div><div class=
=3D"cm-line"><br></div><div class=3D"cm-line">The cost optimisation exercis=
e also demonstrated how machine learning can support more informed concrete=
 mix selection by balancing predicted strength requirements with estimated =
ingredient costs. The developed Meridian Ready-Mix prototype provides a fou=
ndation for data-driven concrete mix evaluation and decision support.</div>=
